+## Current evidence stage (2026-09-23)
+
+Two workstreams, kept in separate paper sections and never merged:
+
+**1. Mobile-robot K/H allocation (the paper's main line).** A three-axis controlled
+scenario-difficulty ladder (182 scenes, tune seeds 1--3 and test seeds 11--20, disjoint)
+was generated and its pre-registration frozen with file hashes before any comparison roll
+(`research_artifacts/kh_scene_strata_2026-09-23/prereg.json` plus two addenda). The nominal
+MPPI baseline was tuned to its own best over a 16-point (K,H) grid and frozen at K=64, H=24.
+
+State of the evidence, stated as it is rather than as planned:
+
+- Claims A and B are **falsified on the tune split** and will be reported as pre-registered
+  failures, not withdrawn (C115, N174).
+- Claim C (horizon-only adaptation collapses and stalls) is a **hypothesis**, frozen in
+  addendum 2 before the test roll, exploratory in origin and confirmatory only on test (C114).
+- Against the **well-tuned** baseline, joint K/H currently shows **no advantage** on tune:
+  worse RMSE in 13 of 14 cells at 1.65x the compute (C115, N180). Two disclosed confounds bound
+  that compute figure and both run **against** our method, so neither can have manufactured the
+  disadvantage in our favour (C117, N184):
+  - the policy **is** charged for compute during training — not via the environment's
+    `lambda_compute` (which is 0) but via the SAC trainer's own reward term
+    `resource = -0.05*sum(measured_e2e_s)`, worth ~17% of the tracking term at the median
+    decision. The earlier claim that compute was "never charged" was false;
+  - the deployed checkpoints were trained with a **5-cycle decision hold** and are evaluated at
+    **1-cycle hold**, and the actor forward pass sits inside the latency meter — so the learned
+    arms pay inference cost 5x more often per episode here than in training.
+  The paper reports 1.65x as a measurement of *this deployed configuration*, never as what
+  learned joint allocation intrinsically costs.
+- The 2520-roll test split is **mid-roll and unadjudicated.** No number from it may be quoted
+  until the sweep, its ablation stage, the 25-roll backfill and `verify_backfill.py` all
+  complete and that verification artifact reads CLEAN.
+
+**2. Preserved-prior discrete-horizon suite (author-side scenario).** Completed with full
+per-episode replay and portable-actor re-run assertions (C113, N182). This is **not** a
+reproduction of Bøhn et al. 2021 — terminal construction, candidate set, training constraints
+and plant all differ — and must never be described as one. It belongs in its own section as a
+method-transfer check, not in the mobile-robot results.
+
+## Reporting boundaries carried into the manuscript
+
+- Per-group tables lead; pooled means never stand in for them.
+- Success is primary; RMSE is never printed without the adjacent success rate.
+- All seeds, levels and axes are reported, including the ones where our method loses.
+- Tune-split numbers are used for selection only and are never reported as results.
+- Measured-delay simulation makes machine exclusivity and fixed concurrency **reproducibility
+  conditions** that belong in the protocol section, not operational trivia (C116).
+- The train/deploy decision-hold mismatch is disclosed in the **method** section with its
+  direction-of-bias argument, whether or not the hold-1 retraining is ever run (C117).
 
